#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:1
msgid "The validation coverage report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`freeports-validate report` walks a repository's grants once and renders "
"what it found in several shapes at a time. This page is that command; "
"what the resulting figures are worth is {doc}`../../guides/grants/index`,"
" and this site's own rendering of them is "
"{doc}`../../validation/report/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:5
msgid "What the command does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:7
msgid ""
"Everything above answers a question about one thing — this file, this "
"person, this methodology. The report answers the question about the "
"repository: **what has been vouched for here, by whom, under what, and "
"does it still hold?**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:11
msgid "It is two subcommands, and the split is the design:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:22
msgid ""
"`collect` walks `validation/*.yaml` once and establishes the facts; every"
" rendering is a **pure function of that JSON**. So a question none of the"
" renderings anticipated is a `jq` expression away rather than a feature "
"request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:31
msgid ""
"Neither needs a key. A report is most often wanted by somebody who did "
"not write the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:33
msgid "What the model holds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "Key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`sources`, `general_methodology`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid ""
"what this run resolved from, and the text every document's `version` is a"
" claim about"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`contributors`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid ""
"one per document: identity, `schema`, `signature`, `version`, how many "
"grants, and whether it is `counted`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`methodologies`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid ""
"name, resolution state, resolved URI and hash, the patterns it declares, "
"one `adoptions` entry per document that adopted it, and its coverage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`grants`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "one per granted file: path, recorded hash, `state`, and `in_scope`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`coverage`, `totals`, `status`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "the repository-wide figures, and one word for the run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:43
msgid ""
"Three of those fields are three-valued rather than two, for the same "
"reason each time — a question that could not be *asked* must not be "
"answered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`grants[].state`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`current`, `changed`, `missing`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`grants[].in_scope`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`true`, `false`, or `null` when the methodology page could not be resolved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`status`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid ""
"`passing`, `failing`, or `inconclusive` — something could not be reached,"
" and nothing was disproved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:52
msgid "How the percentage is arrived at"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:54
msgid ""
"**A methodology that declares no paths contributes no denominator.** "
"There is nothing it could be complete against, and inventing one would "
"put a meaningless percentage on a badge. For one that does declare paths,"
" the denominator is what its patterns match in the working tree — the "
"files it *could* cover — and the numerator is how many of those somebody "
"has granted under it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:59
msgid ""
"**A document that is not intact counts toward nothing.** Coverage is a "
"statement about assurance, and a document whose signature is missing or "
"wrong, or whose `version` is stale, asserts nothing. Its grants are still"
" listed, with the state of the document they came from: an uncounted "
"grant that were also invisible would be a report quietly disagreeing with"
" the repository it describes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:64
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**The repository-wide figure is a union, not a sum.** Adding the per-"
"methodology fractions together would count a file twice as soon as two "
"methodologies declared it, and a badge reading 150% is worse than no "
"badge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:68
msgid "The renderings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`--format`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`--out`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "optional"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "the model. The default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`html`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid ""
"one self-contained page — inline style and script, no fetch of any kind —"
" with the three viewpoints as tabs, matching `who-grants` / `granted-by` "
"/ `granted-with`, a filter box, and every methodology name linking to the"
" text it resolved from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`badges`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "a **directory**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid ""
"`grants-total`, `grants-coverage` and `check-grants`, each as an SVG "
"drawn locally in the shields style and as the shields.io *endpoint* JSON "
"for anyone who would rather fetch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`markdown`, `rst`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "one of seven tables, rewritten in place between two markers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:77
msgid ""
"The Markdown and reStructuredText renderings write **into** a file "
"somebody else wrote, between markers you paste where the table should go:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:90
msgid ""
"Rewriting is idempotent: running it twice changes nothing. A file with no"
" marker pair is an **error** naming the markers, never an append — where "
"a coverage table belongs in a README is a judgement about that README, "
"and a command that guessed would put one under a licence notice and then "
"keep it there for ever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:95
msgid ""
"Nothing the report produces carries a timestamp. A date would make every "
"regeneration a diff saying nothing had changed, which is how a generated "
"block stops being regenerated. What a reader wants to know is what the "
"repository says now, which running the command again tells them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:99
msgid "The seven tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:101
msgid ""
"The HTML page shows three viewpoints as tabs. A Markdown or "
"reStructuredText file cannot have tabs, so it holds **one** table, chosen"
" with `--table`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:104
msgid ""
"There are seven. The repository has three dimensions — file, contributor,"
" methodology — and a lookup is a choice of two of them: group by the "
"first, list the second. Taken in every order that is six, which is "
"exactly what the three lookup subcommands are with and without their "
"flag. The seventh is the summary, and it is the default, so every "
"invocation written before `--table` existed still means what it meant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`--table`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "The same view as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`summary` *(default)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "one line per methodology: its grants, its coverage, who adopted it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`file-contributor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`who-grants <file>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`file-methodology`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`who-grants -m <file>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`contributor-methodology`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`granted-by <contributor>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`contributor-file`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`granted-by -f <contributor>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`methodology-file`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`granted-with <methodology>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`methodology-contributor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md
msgid "`granted-with -c <methodology>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:120
msgid ""
"The name reads as *grouped by the first, listing the second*, and each "
"table says in its own heading which invocation it is the written-down "
"form of — so a reader who has learned the lookups does not have to learn "
"a second vocabulary for the same repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:124
msgid ""
"Each is three columns, one row per distinct pair, with the group key "
"repeated down the first column rather than blanked. Joining the other "
"dimension into one cell is what the lookup subcommands print on a "
"terminal, and it stops being readable the moment a methodology covers "
"several hundred files. The third column is the state of the grants that "
"pair stands for — almost always one word, and two when two documents "
"disagree about the same file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:130
msgid ""
"The `(!)` and `(?)` marks are the ones `granted-by` and its two siblings "
"already print, and they go on the **listed** item, never on the group "
"key: what is out of scope is the *pair*, so marking a heading would split"
" one methodology into two the moment one of its grants left scope. A "
"legend line appears under the table only when a mark actually appears on "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:135
msgid "Rendering several things out of one walk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:137
msgid ""
"A repository that keeps a README, six tables and three badges current has"
" nine artefacts to write, and collecting nine times would resolve every "
"methodology page nine times for an answer that cannot have changed in "
"between. `--model` renders a model gathered earlier instead of walking "
"again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:149
msgid ""
"`--model -` reads the model from a pipe, so `collect | report --model -` "
"works as well. A `--model` naming a file that is not there is an "
"**error**, deliberately not a reason to walk the repository: a run that "
"quietly answered a different question from the one asked is the failure "
"this whole command exists to prevent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:154
msgid "What a repository gets for free"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/coverage-report.md:156
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`freeports-dev init-format-repo` creates all nine of those, already "
"filled, plus the hook that keeps them current — see {ref}`what-init-"
"format-repo-writes`. So the usual answer to \"how do I set this up\" is "
"that it is already set up."
msgstr ""

